  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilience capacity and Climate-Smart Agriculture for the ethnic minority communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Luoi is one of two mountainous areas of Th&#x1EEB;a Thi&#xEA;n-Hu&#x1EBF; province in Central Vietnam. Given the forest degradation, the barren hills, and steep slopes, the area is vulnerable to climate change with negative effects on the livelihoods of ethnic minorities. To minimize the negative impacts of climate change, the project enhanced adaptive capacity for ethnic minority communities. To do so, the project raised local people&#x2019;s awareness of climate change impacts and climate-smart agriculture. It further supported market accessibility of the products deriving from the improved climate-smart agriculture.</narrative>
  </description>
